            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance has now driven the equivalent of a full marathon on Mars (26.2 miles / 42.195 km).** NASA reported the rover hit the milestone on its **1,890th sol** of the mission, and an **MRO/HiRISE orbital image (June 13, 2026)** shows the rover as a tiny speck plus the winding tracks from its route west of Jezero Crater (in an area the team calls **“Arbot”**).【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance recently imaged Earth disappearing behind Mars’s moon Phobos.** NASA published a set of Mastcam‑Z images from **July 2, 2026** showing Earth as a moving point of light that becomes occulted by **Phobos**, with the related feature/article posted **Aug. 5, 2026**.【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\n- **Earlier this year, Perseverance completed the first “AI-planned” drive on another planet.** NASA/JPL described how a **vision-capable generative AI** was used to select rover waypoints (a task normally done by human planners), and Perseverance successfully executed those AI-generated routes during tests in **Dec. 2025** (announced **Jan. 30, 2026**).【5:4†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest news” as *mission milestones*, *science discoveries*, or *new images*, I can narrow it further.",
